WEBVTT

00:00:09,140 --> 00:00:17,060
Are there any issues with adding Fend-Bend-Dissol protocol to my current Supplement Protocol?

00:00:19,730 --> 00:00:25,250
Typically, there's no issues if a person wanted to add Fend-Bend-Dissol to their protocol,

00:00:25,250 --> 00:00:34,850
or if they wanted to add Ivermectin to their protocol, except that which we've talked about in the past,

00:00:34,850 --> 00:00:40,130
you'd want to get a complete metabolic panel done on a more regular basis.

00:00:41,090 --> 00:00:46,050
So, you want to look at both your liver markers and your kidney markers,

00:00:46,050 --> 00:00:52,530
because now you're taking a drug. So, it's not a very high dose if Fend-Bend-Dissol is to dose

00:00:52,530 --> 00:00:59,650
that a 10-pound dog would take. Still, it's a drug. It's a medication that can be difficult

00:00:59,650 --> 00:01:08,290
for your liver to process. So, a lot of people that have liver issues, or if you have genetic issues

00:01:08,290 --> 00:01:14,290
with your liver, you don't process certain drugs very well, and it can cause an elevation

00:01:14,290 --> 00:01:20,610
of your AST, ALT, and alkaline phosphatase. So, you want to look at those. You can have issues with

00:01:21,330 --> 00:01:25,970
your kidney markers as well. So, you want to make sure that you're keeping an eye on that.

00:01:28,610 --> 00:01:34,290
So, as long as you are willing to get more regular blood work, or what's more regular,

00:01:34,290 --> 00:01:39,250
well, get some blood work before you start that, so we can see a baseline of those markers,

00:01:39,810 --> 00:01:46,530
and maybe then a month in after doing that protocol, or if you're having any increased symptoms

00:01:46,530 --> 00:01:51,970
of like pain in your liver or anything, get another blood test to make sure you don't have a spike

00:01:51,970 --> 00:01:56,690
of those markers. So, if you could keep those markers within balance, don't see any problem

00:01:56,690 --> 00:02:02,930
in adding those therapies to your current protocol. So, if the question is, is Fend-Bend-Dissol

00:02:03,010 --> 00:02:08,370
or Iverback could negatively affect the supplements I'm taking, the answer would be no.

00:02:09,010 --> 00:02:16,290
So, in that sense, there's no issue with adding those. Their only issue is that it could affect

00:02:16,290 --> 00:02:27,090
your liver, so you want to make sure you keep an eye on that.

